      "title": "Invoice Service: Troubleshooting HTTP 403 and Role-Based Access Issues",
      "content_summary": "Covers common causes for access denied errors, incorrect role application, and data visibility issues in the Invoice Service, focusing on RBAC and policy configurations.",
      "content_body": "When agents encounter HTTP 403 errors or reports of users seeing wrong tenant data, start by verifying the user's current role assignments within the Invoice Service admin console. Misapplied conditional access policies or stale role caches are frequent culprits, often resulting from recent configuration changes by the customer. Check if the user's permissions align with the required scopes for the specific invoice actions they are attempting. If the issue persists, review the audit logs for policy evaluation failures, which may indicate a conflict between global and tenant-specific rules. Typically, resolving these issues requires a configuration change to update the permission set or correct the policy misconfiguration."
